claimed: intent-embedding-choice — promoted ahead of distillation by the learning curve, which showed the probe and the centroid flattening together at 32 examples: a signal ceiling, not a capacity one. Every tier above 80% goes through ONE embedding model, and the Russian arm (0.741 against English 0.929) is plausibly that model rather than anything in this code. Put a second embedding behind the same seam and re-run the bake-off and the per-language table. Three outcomes, all worth having: a better embedding lifts everything and the ceiling was the vectoriser; it lifts Russian only and the gap was multilingual quality; it changes nothing and the ceiling is the TASK, which would make the 86.7% a fact about four overlapping classes rather than about any classifier.
